# Force binary handling (no LF<->CRLF normalization) for file types that
# are byte-exact by construction. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on
# Windows silently rewrites embedded `\n` bytes to `\r\n` on checkout for
# any file it doesn't detect as binary via its NUL-byte heuristic - which
# corrupts hand-crafted / structurally-precise binary formats like PDF
# (byte offsets in the xref table and stream /Length values go stale)
# without `git status` ever reporting the file as modified.
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
